From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:58:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: sleeping hoppers keep their counters and the
 throttle

performance.sleeping-block-entities.enabled, two fixes to patch 0025:
- The sleeping test now comes after cooldownTime-- and tickedGameTime:
  a sleeping hopper keeps both as if awake. Before, a hopper woken by an
  insert had a stale tickedGameTime (the pushing hopper reads it to set
  the cooldown of its target) and a cooldown counted from when it fell
  asleep: its first transfer was off by up to 8 ticks, which breaks
  hopper clocks and sorters.
- The two options are now independent: with performance.hopper.throttling
  on (the default), an awake hopper still runs once every throttling-ticks
  when sleeping is on too. Patch 0025 said "On, the throttle is skipped":
  no longer so.
Off, the code is the vanilla + throttle code, plus one static boolean read.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
index 84e799f01ef7e48efe7a7f8cc3c3501564807d95..27a1bfbb76aee7ca1479118782894bc9f6bf638f 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
@@ -153,15 +153,13 @@ public class HopperBlockEntity extends RandomizableContainerBlockEntity implemen
         // world share one due tick, which turns vanilla's smooth per-tick load into a single spike
         // every `ticks` ticks. Offsetting by the position hash keeps the same average cost and the
         // same per-hopper interval, but spreads the hoppers evenly over the window.
-        final boolean sleeping = dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.sleepingBlockEntitiesEnabled; // BTCCore - performance.sleeping-block-entities: replaces the throttle below when on
-        if (sleeping) {
-            if (entity.btc$nap.asleep()) return;
-        } else
+        final boolean sleeping = dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.sleepingBlockEntitiesEnabled; // BTCCore - performance.sleeping-block-entities
         if (dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.hopperThrottlingEnabled
             && Math.floorMod(level.getGameTime() + Long.hashCode(pos.asLong()),
                              dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.hopperThrottlingTicks) != 0) return;
         entity.cooldownTime--;
         entity.tickedGameTime = level.getGameTime();
+        if (sleeping && entity.btc$nap.asleep()) return; // BTCCore - performance.sleeping-block-entities: after the two counters, kept as if awake - a hopper pushing into this one reads tickedGameTime, and the first transfer once woken is on the vanilla beat
         if (!entity.isOnCooldown()) {
             entity.setCooldown(0);
             entity.btc$keepAwake = false; // BTCCore - performance.sleeping-block-entities
